  "markdown": "## Interest Rate Parity and Currency Depreciation

- **Interest rate differential**: When one bond offers a higher interest rate than another, the extra return is offset by an expected **depreciation of the currency** in which the higher‑interest bond is denominated.
- **Currency expectation**: The anticipated fall in the value of that currency serves to neutralize the advantage of the higher interest rate.
